  "period_note": "Year-end position from ONE Bank Limited's FY2022 Annual Report, Solo basis. Provision surplus/(deficit) of (10,244.081m) is this report's own contemporaneous figure (also reproduced identically in the FY2023 report's comparative column - no restatement of this particular figure at this step). MAJOR RESTATEMENT (identified via the FY2024 report, see FY2023 note and sources.json): this year's closing Total Assets (314,841.324m) and Total Shareholders' Equity (18,379.799m) were later restated upward, in the FY2024 Annual Report's IAS-8 three-column presentation (as the 01.01.2023 opening balance), to 318,788.927m and 22,057.158m respectively - driven overwhelmingly by a 'Surplus in Profit & Loss Account' (retained earnings) restatement from 1,119.630m to 4,796.989m (+3,677.359m), far larger than any single year's profit. FY2022's own reported net profit after tax (1,391.852m) was NOT itself restated (only the FY2023 P&L was restated under IAS 8's minimum comparative requirement) - the equity effect flows through a direct prior-period retained-earnings adjustment. Contemporaneous FY2022 figures are retained throughout this dataset per 'prefer contemporaneous'; see sources.json for full figures and the FY2023 note for the parallel FY2023 restatement.",
